{"name":"Orange Juice","hex":"#ff7f00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange juice","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The juice of squeezed oranges; used as a beverage or in cocktails. (This entry is a translation hub.)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange_juice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange juice","blocks":[{"text":"Orange juice is a primarily liquid extract of the orange tree fruit, produced by squeezing or reaming oranges. It comes in several different varieties, including blood orange, navel oranges, valencia orange, clementine, and tangerine. As well as variations in oranges used, some varieties include differing amounts of juice vesicles, known as \"pulp\" in American English, and \"(juicy) bits\" in British English. These vesicles contain the juice of the orange and can be left in or removed during the manufacturing process. How juicy these vesicles are depend upon many factors, such as species, variety, and season. In American English, the beverage name is often abbreviated as OJ."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Orangejuice.jpg/330px-Orangejuice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_juice","wikidata":"Q219059"},{"title":"Orange (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"The orange, also called sweet orange to distinguish it from the bitter orange, is the fruit of a tree in the family Rutaceae. Botanically, this is the hybrid Citrus × sinensis, between the pomelo and the mandarin orange. The chloroplast genome, and therefore the maternal line, is that of pomelo. Hybrids of the sweet orange form later types of mandarin and the grapefruit. The sweet orange has had its full genome sequenced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg/330px-Oranges_-_whole-halved-segment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(fruit)","wikidata":"Q13191"},{"title":"Orange Juice (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Juice were a Scottish jangle pop band founded in the Glasgow suburb of Bearsden in 1976. Initially known as the Nu-Sonics, they changed their name to Orange Juice in 1979, and took inspiration from contemporary punk bands including Subway Sect, Television, and Buzzcocks and 1960s acts such as the Byrds and the Velvet Underground. Musically, the band brought together styles and genres that often appeared incongruous, for example, country, disco and punk. Though their line-up changed numerous times, lead singer and guitarist Edwyn Collins was a constant presence and the 'face' of the band."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Juice_(band)","wikidata":"Q1781317"},{"title":"Juice","blocks":[{"text":"Juice is a drink made from the extraction or pressing of the natural liquid contained in fruit and vegetables. It can also refer to liquids that are flavored with concentrate or other biological food sources like meat or seafood, such as clam juice. Juice is commonly consumed as a beverage or used as an ingredient or flavoring in foods or other beverages, such as smoothies. Juice emerged as a popular beverage choice after the development of pasteurization methods enabled its preservation without using fermentation. The largest fruit juice consumers are New Zealand and Colombia. Fruit juice consumption on average increases with a country's income level."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Orange_juice_1.jpg/330px-Orange_juice_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juice","wikidata":"Q8492"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Orange_Juice_Pulp.jpg/500px-Orange_Juice_Pulp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Orange_Juice_Pulp.jpg/500px-Orange_Juice_Pulp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of orange juice with pulp","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrange_Juice_Pulp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg/500px-Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg/1280px-Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg/500px-Mexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mexico City merchant with his freshly squeezed orange juice, March 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMexico_City_merchant_with_his_freshly_squeezed_orange_juice_March_2010.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/1280px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of blood orange juice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABloodorange1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w